</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CoT with </span><math id="S3.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> samples and majority voting </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a><span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S3.T1.1.6.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.2pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T1.1.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Very High</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">20.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20.0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.1.6.5.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T1.1.6.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> simultaneous inference passes </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.T1.1.6.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a><span id="S3.T1.1.6.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S3.T1.1.6.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>The Composite Objective Function <math id="S3.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The PPN is trained to maximize the expected value of a composite, resource-penalized reward <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(a_{t},s_{t})=\alpha\cdot\text{Accuracy}(a_{t},Q)-\beta\cdot\text{Computational Cost}(a_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Accuracy</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Computational Cost</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(a_{t},s_{t})=\alpha\cdot\text{Accuracy}(a_{t},Q)-\beta\cdot\text{Computational Cost}(a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Accuracy}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Accuracy</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Accuracy}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is binary, and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Computational Cost}\in\mathbb{R}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Computational Cost</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Computational Cost}\in\mathbb{R}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is the observed cost proxy <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The hyperparameters <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> establish the optimal utility function for the desired trade-off, functioning similarly to coefficients in adaptive control systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
By embedding cost <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> as a penalty, the PPN learns the optimal soft resource threshold based on the expected accuracy gain, ensuring optimal utility maximization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Methodology: The Prompt Policy Network (PPN)</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>PPN Architecture and Input Feature Engineering</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The PPN is designed for efficiency and utilizes a small, frozen language model encoder to generate the low-dimensional feature vector <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> (state <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.
The success of the PPN critically relies on the encoder’s ability to extract features that correlate strongly with the required reasoning complexity.
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is fed into a lightweight Feedforward Network (FFN), which branches into a Policy Head <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (outputting <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> over strategies <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>) and a Value Head <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> (outputting the estimated expected composite reward <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s)</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="350.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 649.52 350.02" width="649.52"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,350.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(299.66,0) translate(0,335.69)"><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -51.63 -13.78 h 103.26 v 27.56 h -103.26 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -47.02 -3.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="94.03"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (Input Query)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -115.07 -89.69 h 230.15 v 27.56 h -230.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -110.46 -79.02)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="92.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Frozen Encoder </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a><span id="S4.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -56.12 -165.6 h 112.23 v 27.56 h -112.23 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -51.5 -154.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.13em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.26em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.7" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="104.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F1.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (State Vector)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -93.27 -253.32 h 186.54 v 39.37 h -186.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -88.66 -236.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="142.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">PPN (</span><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta},V_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta},V_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F1.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">) (Policy Network)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 212.49 -247.42 h 86.61 v 27.56 h -86.61 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 230.04 -237.22)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="36.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Select </span><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 174 -335.14 h 163.59 v 39.37 h -163.59 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 178.61 -318.56)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="156.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Target SLM (Environment)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;" fill="#E6E6E6" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path d="M -299.1 -247.42 h 86.61 v 27.56 h -86.61 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -284.07 -237.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="47.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reward </span><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -14.33 L 0 -57.98"></path><g transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -57.98)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -90.24 L 0 -133.89"></path><g transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -133.89)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -166.15 L 0 -209.8"></path><g transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -209.8)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 93.82 -233.64 L 208.34 -233.64"></path><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 208.34 -233.64)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 112.71 -225.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.04em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="35.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Policy <math id="S4.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 255.79 -247.97 L 255.79 -291.62"></path><g transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 255.79 -291.62)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 260.96 -274.3)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.56)" width="84.29"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Execute Prompt</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.45 -315.45 L -208.41 -234.38"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.9782 0.20767 -0.20767 -0.9782 -208.41 -234.38)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -97.19 -266.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.56)" width="39.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*},C^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*},C^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.F1.pic1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -211.93 -233.64 L -97.42 -233.64"></path><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -97.42 -233.64)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -177.13 -228.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.12em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="48.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Feedback</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>PPN Architecture and Lightweight RL Optimization Loop. The PPN takes the encoded query state <math id="S4.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, selects a strategy <math id="S4.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and receives feedback (<math id="S4.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>) from the LLM execution environment.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Policy Optimization via Constrained PPO-Clip</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The PPN policy <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is trained using Proximal Policy Optimization with Clipping (PPO-Clip), an on-policy algorithm known for its stability.
The PPO-Clip objective function <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{CLIP}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{CLIP}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is adapted to maximize the expected composite reward:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{CLIP}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\min(r_{t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{t},\text{clip}(r_{t}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\hat{A}_{t})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{CLIP}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\min(r_{t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{t},\text{clip}(r_{t}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\hat{A}_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\theta_{k}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\theta_{k}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability ratio, and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the clipping hyperparameter.
The advantage estimate <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated based on the composite reward <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{t}=R(s_{t},a_{t})-V_{\phi}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{t}=R(s_{t},a_{t})-V_{\phi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
To ensure robust exploration across the action space, an entropy regularization term, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma H(\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma H(\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, is added to the objective, which helps balance exploration and exploitation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>PPN Training Algorithm</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The training involves iteratively collecting data by executing the selected prompt strategy on the target LLM and optimizing the policy via PPO updates.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Prompt Policy Network (PPN) Training Algorithm (PPO Adaptation)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0},\phi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0},\phi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (PPN parameters), <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta,\epsilon,\gamma,K_{epochs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta,\epsilon,\gamma,K_{epochs}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> episode <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              Sample batch <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\{Q_{1},\ldots,Q_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\{Q_{1},\ldots,Q_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from Task Dataset

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Q_{i}}\leftarrow\text{Encoder}(Q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Encoder</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Q_{i}}\leftarrow\text{Encoder}(Q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Encode query state features <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta_{old}}(a|F_{Q_{i}})\leftarrow\text{PPN}_{\theta_{old}}(F_{Q_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>PPN</mtext><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta_{old}}(a|F_{Q_{i}})\leftarrow\text{PPN}_{\theta_{old}}(F_{Q_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
