:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="13.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F2.pic1.19" class="ltx_text">90</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Efficiency-Accuracy Pareto Front (Conceptual Visualization). Fixed strategies (ZS, CoT, SC) occupy discrete, sub-optimal points.
PPN policies (varying <math id="S5.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>) lie on a superior Pareto front, confirming maximum utility maximization.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Adaptive Policy Efficacy and Strategy Distribution</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table 2 presents comparative performance analysis across critical operational regimes.</p>
</div>
